  "step_3": "The decision reason evaluates the minimum probability of each lottery and prefers the one with the lower minimum probability (Lottery B). However, the individual’s justification focuses on risk aversion and the worst-case outcome (loss), not on the minimum probability. The individual did not mention probabilities at all in their reasoning, nor did they refer to the magnitude or frequency of probabilities. Instead, they prioritized safety and absence of loss. Therefore, the information considered by the individual (risk, worst-case outcome) does not align with the decision reason (minimum probability). The rule applied by the individual (avoiding loss, preferring certainty) is inconsistent with the reason’s rule (preferring lower minimum probability). Thus, the decision reason was not used. The final assessment is 0.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
